    "result_text": "The build passes. The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` field following the codebase's established \"deriver + MapStruct expression\" pattern:\n\n1. **`OwnerSegmentDeriver.java`** (new) \u2014 a standalone helper with `ownerSegment(int membershipLevel, String locality)`:\n   - TIER = `PREMIUM` when `membershipLevel >= 3`, else `STANDARD`\n   - AREA = `METRO` when locality \u2208 {NSW, VIC, QLD}, else `REGIONAL`\n   - Returns `<TIER>_<AREA>`\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `ownerSegment` string property to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` has the field).\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 registered the deriver in `uses`/`imports` and added a `@Mapping` expression that composes the existing derivers:\n   ```java\n   OwnerSegmentDeriver.ownerSegment(\n       MembershipPointsDeriver.effectiveMembershipLevel(owner),\n       LocalityDeriver.locality(owner.getCustomerCode()))\n   ```\n\nThis reuses `effectiveMembershipLevel` and `LocalityDeriver.locality` (same source used for the `locality` field), so the segment stays consistent with the owner's reported membership level and locality. Both acceptance tests (`STANDARD_METRO` for Sydney/NSW, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown city) pass.",
